  "text": "\n     Ballot Clerks Needed for Election Year 2026 • Farmington, NH \n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     About   \t\t\t \n     Departments   \t\t\t \n     Boards & Commissions   \t\t\t \n     Find It Fast   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \nHome \n                News Flash\nBallot Clerks Needed for Election Year 2026 \nNews Flash \n            Ballot Clerks Needed for Election Year 2026\n                Home\n                Posted on September 04, 2026 \nBALLOT CLERKS NEEDED \nfor Election Year 2026 \nState General Election: November 3 rd \nMust be a resident of Farmington. \nRegistered Democrats and Republicans preferred. Undeclared clerks must have a voting history of one party more than the other to be considered. \n1-2 hour training about 2 weeks before each election. \n7:30 AM – at least 10:00 PM \nBreakfast, Lunch, and Dinner are provided. \nRegular coverage provided for meals and breaks. \nEarn $100.00 for the day. \nPlease call (603 755-3657), email ( tctc@farmington.nh.us ), or stop into the Town Clerk/Tax Collector's office at 356 Main Street for more information. \nRelated News \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTown of Farmington Breezeline Agreement\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHome\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosted on September 29, 2026 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFarmington Accepting Proposals For Senior Center Painting/Trim Repair\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHome\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosted on September 28, 2026 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFarmington Town-Owned Vehicle & Equipment Auction\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHome\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosted on September 24, 2026 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLilac State Solar Project Information\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tHome\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosted on November 03, 2025 | Last Updated on September 24, 2026\n\t\t\t FAQs \r\n\t\t\t Minutes & Agendas \r\n\t\t\t Online Dog, Motor Vehicle, & Vital Records \r\n\t\t\t Online Tax and Water/Sewer Payment \r\n\t\t\t Building Permits \r\n\t\t